  "strategy": "Approach and rationale: \n\nWe address the problem of minimizing the maximum shift-overlap of a step function on [0,2] with integral 1. The previous implementation used multi-resolution refinement combined with subgradient-based and basin-hopping optimization. Our key improvement is to replace the coordinate descent with momentum-based gradient optimization, incorporate early stopping mechanics, and introduce multi-start strategy from diverse generators. This new approach maintains active constraints throughout optimization and reduces local minima trapping.\n\nMathematical specification: \n\nMinimize T_max = max_k \u222b_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx s.t. \u222b_0^2 h(x) dx = 1, 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1.\n\nDiscrete equivalent using convex combination: minimize (1/(2n)) * max_lag( correlation[l] ) s.t. sum(h_i) = n (implicitly handled via scaling).\n\nImplementation procedure:\n\n1. Setup:\n   - Input: grid function h from parent solution (n=200)\n   - Convert to [0,1] projection if needed\n   - Initialize time tracking\n\n2. Optimization stages:\n   a. Constraint embedding:\n        h_projected = project_h(h)\n        Augmented objective: H_ij = h_i * (1-h_j + \u03b5_i)  \u03b5_i ~ N(0, \u03c3^2)\n\n   b. Gradient computation:\n        \u2207_i = (sum_j H_ij * shift_penalty) + integral_penalty\n        Where shift_penalty emphasizes large contributions from \\|i-j\\|=k_max\n\n   c. Momentum-based updates:\n        v_i,t+1 = \u03b2 * v_i,t + \u03b7 * (clip(\u2207_i, -c, c))\n        h_i,t+1 = clamp( h_i,t + v_i,t+1, 0, 1)\n\n   d. Multi-start diversification:\n        Start from: random, binary-patterned, symmetry-enforced variants\n\n   e. Early stopping:\n        Terminate if \u2207 max/mini < tol or no improvement 10 steps\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n\n- Main strategy: Momentum-based optimization with structured multi-start diversification\n- Hyperparameters: momentum=0.95, learning_rate=0.0015, shift_penalty_factor=0.8\n- Diversification strategies:\n  - Uniform random initialization\n  - Symmetry-enforced (even/odd pattern)\n  - Reference pattern learning from current best\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n\n- Time allocation: ~70% on first optimization, 30% on refinement\n- Graceful degradation: apply fallback projection if NaN values\n- Constraints: enforce via penalty and projection at each step\n- Early termination: reduce learning_rate by 1.5x if no progress\n\nValidation and return contract:\n\n- Project solution to valid space via clip and sum adjustment\n- Compute final c5_bound using only exact correlation\n- Return (h_values, c5_bound, n_points) where n_points is current resolution\n\nNote: The algorithm maintains integral constraint as active constraint via dual embedding.",
